-- KFGQPC Hafs Uthmanic Data for Smart Phone
-- Version: 0.8
-- Updated Date: 2022-06-30 
-- Updated: 6.0
  - Correct some words by remove spaces between them in 43 places. i.e: sura:2, page:12, aya:77  	
  – Modifying Encoding of “hafs_smart_v8.csv” file from UTF-8 to UTF-8-BOM
  - Modifying some Jozz numbers in data files such as Sura An-Naml(27) Aya(56-59) from (19) to (20)
  - Removing Kashida from different places in aya_text_emlaey column
  - Adding line_start column and line_end column in data table
  - Modifying Sura Name (الشُّورى) instead of (الشُّوري)
   

It includes two folders:
1- Uthmanic_font
	- It contains font file and whole Qur'an data in MS document file
2- Uthmanic_data
	- It contains files for developers.
	
Columns:
--------
1-  id (int):	 			  Auto_increment Number
2-  jozz (int):		 		  Jozz Number
3-  sura_no (int):			  Sura Number
4-  sura_name_en (varchar):	  Sura Name in English
5-  sura_name_ar (varchar):	  Sura Name in Arabic
6-  page (int):				  Page Number
7-  line_start (int):		  Start Line of Aya
8-  line_end (int):			  End Line of Aya
9-  aya_no (int):			  Aya Number
10- aya_text (text):		  Text of the Aya in UthmanicHafs Smart unicode
11- aya_text_emlaey (text):	  Emlaey Text of the Aya used for search purpose

Available Data Formats:
======================

1. hafs_smart.csv
   --------------
   - Format: CSV (Comma Separated Values)
   - Size: 6,238 lines
   - Content: Complete Quran text in CSV format with all 11 columns
   - Usage: Can be imported into spreadsheet applications or databases
   - Encoding: UTF-8 with Unicode support for Arabic text

2. hafs_smart.json
   ---------------
   - Format: JSON (JavaScript Object Notation)
   - Size: 81,071 lines
   - Content: Complete Quran data in JSON array format
   - Structure: Array of objects, each representing one verse
   - Usage: Perfect for web applications and APIs
   - Features: Easy parsing in JavaScript and other programming languages

3. hafs_smart.html
   ---------------
   - Format: HTML Table
   - Size: 87,326 lines
   - Content: Complete Quran data displayed as HTML table
   - Title: "KFGQPC Uthmanic Hafs Smart v8 Data"
   - Usage: Can be opened directly in web browsers
   - Features: Formatted table with silver header background

4. hafs_smart.sql
   --------------
   - Format: SQL INSERT Statements
   - Size: 6,241 lines
   - Content: Complete Quran data as SQL INSERT commands
   - Database: Compatible with MySQL/MariaDB/PostgreSQL
   - Usage: Direct import into SQL databases
   - Date: Generated on 2022-06-30

5. hafs_smart.xml
   --------------
   - Format: XML (eXtensible Markup Language)
   - Size: 87,307 lines
   - Content: Complete Quran data in XML structure
   - Structure: <DATA> root with <ROW> elements for each verse
   - Usage: Perfect for data exchange and integration
   - Features: Well-formed XML with proper encoding

6. hafs_smart.xlsx
   ---------------
   - Format: Microsoft Excel Spreadsheet
   - Content: Complete Quran data in Excel format
   - Usage: Can be opened with Excel, LibreOffice Calc, etc.
   - Features: Supports advanced filtering and analysis

